From adae0d677a17b4b9b4838fe11759b08951ff6799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:54:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] A synth loaded into a kit row: no stale pointers, no E412
 on knob learn (#4518, #4951)

From the open upstream PRs #4951 and #4518, adapted to 62a516c2:
- performLoadSynthToKit() takes the backed-up ParamManager with stealInto (no empty backup entry
  left for Sound::learnKnob() to walk: E412), and setDrum(..., false) frees the row's old main
  collections instead of leaking them (#4951; null check added).
- The view is re-pointed at the new drum after the swap; Kit::drumRemoved() clears the view's
  cache; SoundEditor::exitCompletely() clears all its current* pointers (#4518 family A).
- Browser::backButtonAction() cancels the BACK_MENU_EXIT timer when its press exits (the root
  folder), and LoadSongUI::exitAction() is guarded against running twice (#4518 family B, a
  precaution: not reproduced).

Test (beta-1.3/tests): kitrow_emu.py; on 62a516c2 the view points at the freed drum and LEARN +
a gold knob freezes with E412.
